data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrocfw — mission \\\"greet, tested\\\" — report\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three mission criteria are satisfied:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` defines `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name (`greet(\\\"World\\\")`) and the empty\\n   string (`greet(\\\"\\\")`), using `unittest`.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0.\\n\\n## How it was produced\\n\\n- Dispatched the full spec to `dev` in one dispatch (d002), including the\\n  exact verification command to run before replying.\\n- `dev` implemented `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py`, reported all\\n  criteria met, and committed to its own branch\\n  (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `1928a68`).\\n\\n## Independent verification (not just trusting the report)\\n\\n- Fetched `dev`'s branch (`refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`) into the\\n  orchestrator's clone.\\n- Diffed against the campaign base (`1053761f`): only the two expected files\\n  were added — `src/greet.py` (+2 lines) and `tests/test_greet.py` (+19\\n  lines). No extra files or unrelated changes.\\n- Read both files directly: `greet()` implementation matches the spec exactly;\\n  the test file imports `greet` from `src/greet.py` and has two test cases —\\n  one normal name, one empty string.\\n- Built an isolated git worktree at `dev`'s commit and ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` independently (not reusing dev's\\n  reported output): `Ran 2 tests in 0.000s — OK`, exit code 0.\\n- Accepted d002 only after this independent verification passed.\\n\\n## Where the work lives\\n\\n- Fast-forward merged dev's commit onto the orchestrator's own branch\\n  (`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`), which now points at\\n  commit `1928a68497e4aa5c492187fdac5f9cc0830a711f`\\n  (\\\"Implement greet(name) with unittest tests (d002)\\\").\\n- This is the only commit beyond the campaign base; the orchestrator's branch\\n  tree differs from base as evidence of delivered work.\\n\\n## Nothing left unmet\\n\\nNo criterion from `mission.md` is outstanding.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

